WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.191 --> 00:00:16.354
Father returned home, Beth's recovery took a turn for the better as she rapidly grew stronger.

2
00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:20.797
In no time she was climbing upstairs and downstairs on her own.

3
00:00:21.698 --> 00:00:25.581
Being with his family again seemed to have the same effect on Father's health as well.

4
00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:31.400
True, he had lost a lot of weight and his body seemed stiff and sore, but his eyes

5
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.341
remained as kind and watchful as ever.

6
00:00:33.361 --> 00:00:38.003
"Shall I continue with the next chapter, or do you want a nap?"

7
00:00:38.303 --> 00:00:41.104
Father asked Beth, who was lying on the sofa listening to him read.

8
00:00:42.085 --> 00:00:46.026
Jo, who was also listening, answered excitedly, "Please carry on.

9
00:00:46.326 --> 00:00:47.587
I want to know what happens!"

10
00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:55.210
Laughing, Beth nodded and said, "I'd like to hear more, too, Father, but only if you're not too

11
00:00:55.270 --> 00:01:01.873
tired." "I never get tired of reading to you, my dear girl," Father said lovingly, as he turned

12
00:01:01.893 --> 00:01:02.953
the page and continued.

13
00:01:02.973 --> 00:01:06.195
"Oh, this color is not right either!"

14
00:01:06.535 --> 00:01:10.797
complained Amy from the corner by the window, where she had set up her easel and was trying

15
00:01:10.817 --> 00:01:12.177
to paint a vase of flowers.

16
00:01:13.478 --> 00:01:17.279
Mother and Meg, smiled at the peacefulness of their family at that moment.

17
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.441
But the peace didn't last long.

18
00:01:20.461 --> 00:01:23.742
"Oh, I can't believe she's here!"

19
00:01:24.182 --> 00:01:26.423
Amy suddenly cried as she glanced out the window.

20
00:01:26.443 --> 00:01:28.124
"Who, Amy?"

21
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.582
asked Mother, standing up to look for herself.

22
00:01:31.803 --> 00:01:32.584
"Aunt March!

23
00:01:32.944 --> 00:01:38.208
Thank goodness, she didn't bring that annoying parrot," said Amy, screwing the lids back on her paints.

24
00:01:39.649 --> 00:01:46.535
Unseen by their children, Mother and Father exchanged wordless glances that meant "get ready" for this unexpected visit.

25
00:01:48.137 --> 00:01:51.940
Mother opened the door for Aunt March as she strolled into the house as if she owned it.

26
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.784
"Oh, there you are," she said, catching sight of Father.

27
00:01:57.612 --> 00:01:58.572
"How are you, Aunt?"

28
00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.793
he asked graciously as he stood to give her a kiss on the cheek.

29
00:02:01.813 --> 00:02:10.035
"You go off to war at your age, get sick, take away the children's mother, meanwhile your small

30
00:02:10.135 --> 00:02:17.197
one gets scarlet fever and nearly dies," snapped Aunt March, "so that the youngest, as adorable as she

31
00:02:17.397 --> 00:02:25.459
is" —here Aunt March nodded approvingly at Amy— "is sent over to my care despite my illnesses and

32
00:02:25.539 --> 00:02:27.260
you ask me how I am!"

33
00:02:27.624 --> 00:02:28.304
she concluded.

34
00:02:29.425 --> 00:02:34.548
While Father tried to explain his situation to Aunt March, who demanded that Jo bring a blanket for

35
00:02:34.568 --> 00:02:39.090
her cold knees and ordered hot tea from Meg, Amy announced more visitors to the house.

36
00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.272
"Here come Laurie and Mr.

37
00:02:41.312 --> 00:02:44.373
Brookes," she shouted, waving eagerly out the window.

38
00:02:45.754 --> 00:02:49.096
Cheeks flushing, Meg quickly disappeared into the kitchen to get the tea.

39
00:02:50.497 --> 00:02:54.799
Father stood up, relieved, even for a moment, not to have to listen to his aunt's scolding, and

40
00:02:54.859 --> 00:02:56.380
welcomed the guests into his home.

41
00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.521
Father and Mr.

42
00:02:58.561 --> 00:03:02.823
Brookes had formed a close bond during his sickness, and since then Mr.

43
00:03:02.863 --> 00:03:05.264
Brookes had become a regular visitor to the March home.

44
00:03:06.145 --> 00:03:10.807
As much as Meg tried to appear cool, secretly, she was happy to see John so often.

45
00:03:12.568 --> 00:03:17.070
Her pride might not admit it, but Meg's heart could no longer deny her feelings for him.

46
00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:20.772
"I have something to ask you, sir," Mr.

47
00:03:20.792 --> 00:03:23.534
Brookes said to Father, not realizing that Aunt March was there.

48
00:03:23.554 --> 00:03:25.755
"Who are you?"

49
00:03:26.275 --> 00:03:27.356
asked Aunt March bluntly.

50
00:03:28.244 --> 00:03:34.549
While Father explained, Meg entered with the tea, her hands shaking ever so slightly, causing the china to

51
00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:35.530
rattle on the tray.

52
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:42.836
"Child," Aunt March shrieked at Meg, "I swear you're going to break that cheap tea set if you

53
00:03:42.897 --> 00:03:43.997
clink them any harder!"

54
00:03:44.938 --> 00:03:48.181
Turning a deep red, Meg would have dropped the tray if Mr.

55
00:03:48.241 --> 00:03:51.404
Brookes hadn't sprung up and taken it from her trembling hands.

56
00:03:52.352 --> 00:03:55.434
As Aunt March sipped her tea, she kept one eye on Mr.

57
00:03:55.454 --> 00:04:02.299
Brookes, sensing his obvious attraction to Meg, and the other eye on Meg, who undoubtedly shared the same

58
00:04:02.399 --> 00:04:03.440
feelings toward him.

59
00:04:05.021 --> 00:04:10.225
Meanwhile Jo, oblivious to what was happening, caught sight of Laurie trying to get her attention.

60
00:04:11.086 --> 00:04:15.389
He motioned with his head toward the kitchen, so Jo cautiously got up and crept away.

61
00:04:16.149 --> 00:04:17.730
Laurie joined her a few minutes later.

62
00:04:18.471 --> 00:04:19.071
"What is it?"

63
00:04:19.351 --> 00:04:19.952
Jo asked him.

64
00:04:21.252 --> 00:04:22.933
"Something major is about to happen.

65
00:04:23.313 --> 00:04:25.934
I can't tell you but Laurie began excitedly.

66
00:04:25.954 --> 00:04:29.896
"Then why bother calling me into the kitchen?"

67
00:04:30.316 --> 00:04:31.296
Jo asked irritably.

68
00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:34.398
"To save you the shock," Laurie said.

69
00:04:34.418 --> 00:04:36.659
"From what?"

70
00:04:37.099 --> 00:04:37.599
asked Jo.

71
00:04:37.619 --> 00:04:44.602
"Something major is going to happen that will change your life forever," Laurie said firmly, looking deep into

72
00:04:44.642 --> 00:04:45.262
Jo's eyes.

73
00:04:46.823 --> 00:04:51.797
Then grabbing her arm, he led her back to the living room, where to Jo's horror, the big

74
00:04:51.837 --> 00:04:53.479
event was just taking place.

75
00:04:54.759 --> 00:04:58.202
Mr. Brookes was on his knee in front of Meg and he was holding her hand.

76
00:04:59.102 --> 00:05:00.904
"Margaret March, will you marry me?"

77
00:05:01.364 --> 00:05:03.165
Brookes asked in a gentlemanly manner.

78
00:05:03.185 --> 00:05:05.647
"What is the meaning of this?"

79
00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:07.308
Aunt March demanded.

80
00:05:07.328 --> 00:05:09.369
"This is an outrage!

81
00:05:09.749 --> 00:05:11.070
You are only a child!"

82
00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:16.254
"Aunt March, I don't think this matter concerns you," Father said firmly.

83
00:05:16.274 --> 00:05:19.056
"Of course it concerns me!

84
00:05:19.776 --> 00:05:20.977
I am the head of the family.

85
00:05:21.778 --> 00:05:23.059
You belong to me!

86
00:05:23.659 --> 00:05:25.521
Therefore I have a right to speak!"

87
00:05:25.861 --> 00:05:26.742
she said haughtily.

88
00:05:26.762 --> 00:05:32.287
"I love your grandniece, madam, and I promise to make her as happy and content as she is

89
00:05:32.347 --> 00:05:33.888
now," John said kindly.

90
00:05:35.069 --> 00:05:40.854
Looking him up and down, Aunt March said disdainfully, "You're nothing but a poor tutor.

91
00:05:41.394 --> 00:05:43.276
How can you make this girl happy?"

92
00:05:44.096 --> 00:05:44.617
Poor Mr.

93
00:05:44.657 --> 00:05:48.360
Brookes flushed with embarrassment and anger, but he controlled it admirably.

94
00:05:49.468 --> 00:05:51.229
Surprisingly, it was Meg who spoke up.

95
00:05:51.249 --> 00:05:53.110
"Aunt March!

96
00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.031
I will not allow you to speak to this man in that way.

97
00:05:57.411 --> 00:06:01.273
He is a good kind person who has helped our family when we needed him.

98
00:06:02.213 --> 00:06:03.574
What have you done for us?

99
00:06:04.074 --> 00:06:08.176
You never offered to help Father when he lost his money or even when he was sick.

100
00:06:09.056 --> 00:06:11.537
You never came to visit Beth while she had the fever.

101
00:06:12.498 --> 00:06:16.759
And now you come here and tell me that I can't marry the man who has done nothing

102
00:06:16.799 --> 00:06:18.000
but good for our family?

103
00:06:19.108 --> 00:06:20.569
No! I will not allow it!"

104
00:06:20.969 --> 00:06:24.331
Meg cried, not caring as tears rolled down her cheeks.

105
00:06:25.491 --> 00:06:26.512
Everyone was stunned.

106
00:06:27.452 --> 00:06:29.913
They had never seen Meg react so strongly in her life.

107
00:06:31.094 --> 00:06:38.458
Shaking with anger, Aunt March pointed her walking stick at Meg and threatened, "I warn you, Margaret, if

108
00:06:38.558 --> 00:06:43.240
you marry this man, you will not get a single penny from me when I die!"

109
00:06:44.924 --> 00:06:48.907
Meg took a deep breath and turning her back on Aunt March, she grabbed John's hands and said

110
00:06:48.947 --> 00:06:51.910
to him, "Yes, John Brookes, I will marry you."

111
00:06:53.231 --> 00:06:57.134
Jo felt the ground drop from beneath her and before she knew it, she was lying on the

112
00:06:57.174 --> 00:07:00.216
floor with a circle of worried faces staring down at her.

113
00:07:00.236 --> 00:07:02.318
"Are you all right, Jo?"

114
00:07:02.578 --> 00:07:05.601
Laurie asked, pulling Jo up and giving her a slight shake.

115
00:07:07.142 --> 00:07:10.325
Nodding, Jo said, "Yes, I'm fine."

116
00:07:10.345 --> 00:07:14.088
"Oh, Jo, isn't this wonderful news?"

117
00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.284
Meg said in a breathless voice as she hugged her sister.

118
00:07:17.304 --> 00:07:20.027
"I'm getting married!"

119
00:07:21.189 --> 00:07:23.232
Hearing those words again, Jo fainted.

120
00:07:24.413 --> 00:07:29.140
She hoped she would never wake up from the awful nightmare that was about to unfold.
